ople love but  there's actually a relief too to not see  her in heavy makeup like she is for  guardians of the galaxy or avatar where  she's cgi this is her in her full form  where i was just singing all the time i  want to see this more and katherine  keener as always plays a great villain  here so what works really well about  this film to me is the story right and  that  it has a clear-cut message in it and  that's said towards the end of the film  where we get this great scene where the  two atoms are talking to each other and  the younger adam's saying it's easier to  be angry than to be sad right this is  the whole message of the film and  there's a great line before that where  they're talking about his hate for his  father he's like you hate him because he  died you made yourself hate him so you  didn't miss him dad always had a catch  even if he was tired so  i thought all this was great there was  just certain scenes that really stuck  with me and they did a good job of like  the moment it almost felt like it was  getting too sappy at points it would hit  with some kind of  wittier mark by ryan reynolds or some  action so they they had a nice balance  of tone here and you knew this was  coming scenes like this because there  was really good scenes even just in the  beginning with jennifer garner and ryan  reynolds in the bar and he's talking to  his mom and they had a fun time just  playing around with the time travel in a  way where they didn't obsess about the  time travel itself that really isn't  something they were like oh we gotta get  the logic right it wasn't the point of  the film the time travel is just there  as a plot device to get things going to  where they need to be they actually just  had fun with these characters and again  the message and it was a good plot that  they were trying to destroy time travel  so that felt a little more fresh too but  even this scene it's portrayed so  beautifully by ryan reynolds here when  he's talking to his mom and ryan  reynolds really showing his acting chops  in this film especially dramatic acting  chops and  i love the message it had to here too  about him telling his former self  through all his regrets he's had in life  you know to be good to his mom that his  mom is suffering and that he tells the  mom to tell her son that she has this  sadness in her and that she is  struggling you don't have to be perfect  like all these themes were just clicking  so well in this film and they got their  pass by the end and it really paid off  all this setup with those kind of  moments because it really hit home when  young adam later on  clicks to him and he remembers somewhere  in his brain that his future self told  him to hug his mom extra tight i thought  that was really well done and i also  thought a lot of the action was really  well done here with  keeping it interesting and what really  stood out to me is chasing where they're  getting chased by mia the two atoms and  they're in they're flying and i love  that he stops the jet and then goes but  it had a nice  rhythm to it and it had stakes that were  interesting it wasn't just over  loaded with action here every action  scene was had a little story in it of  who was the target you know who they're  running from and it kept that suspense  up which i thought was really nice but  there was little humorous moments  that were so great and subtle like one  of my favorites was adam is with laura  here and she's meeting young adam for  the first time and she's basically  giving exposition for the film for us to  understand giving it to the older adam  but while she does that she goes here  make sure you eat something young adam  and she hands him a carrot and he just  mouths what the f i thought that was so  funny and it shows already that comic  timing that walker scoble has and how  good he is at it already and one of the  best humorous scenes is when mark  ruffalo comes into the picture and it's  just  always exciting when you see  a scene in film that you feel like  you've never seen before and that's  really here it really stood out was like  so brilliant to me where he's fighting  with the adult adam trying to be nice to  the younger adam and they're both  reacting to their dad at the same time  and he's like why did you grow up to be  an [ __ ] and then he's like i thought  you loved me and then the younger one  responds i do i thought that was just  great and it was great to see  the older adam talked to the younger  adam in front of the dad and how  differently they're trying to react to  him so cool and just again that  moments like this with mark ruffalo and  ryan reynolds just doing awesome with  the improvising clearly with some of the  comedic responses to each other they  probably took so many takes trying  different things they still brought in  again  nice heartwarming things touching things  to make those payoffs earn like the  scene where they're having the catch at  the end and they disappear was great and  that had to be earned by having moments  where  you know he's asking his dad to be a  father not just a scientist and again  like that picnic scene which really was  the best to me with the young adam  talking to the older adam you know about  not being mad anymore and it's just even  a heartbreaking moment when you see  young adam wants to tell his father so  bad that he dies i thought that was  great it's not spielberg level but it's  clearly inspired where you have  such good adventure here action but  a lot of heart and  i love the pace of this film too i  thought it constantly was moving it was  doing what it needed to do especially  for its target audience right that  someone wants just to escape but feel  warmth from it but also a lot of  laughing it was just your classic  feel-good blockbuster that really was  effective in what it was trying to do  now  only criticisms i might have is that  maybe the story line with zoe saldana's  character of lauren didn't get enough  time and then it makes me think maybe it  wasn't even needed you know i think  it is a nice touch and it's great to  always have her in a film but  you know it kind of just was there to  set up that big moment at the end where  he finds her again which was awesome but  i felt like maybe it was just adding  another thing they probably didn't even  need because they already had this  strong story with the dad and that you  know we really in the day to get much  time with laura now  you know maybe if there's a sequel it  will be more justified but again maybe  if you look at it a different way that  maybe that wasn't totally needed it was  still effective but definitely needed a  little more time there because i still  barely felt like i knew laura so maybe  the payoff didn't feel as strong and i  like with the villain of mia that they  gave her a scene to talk about how all  her life is this mission right with the  time travel and that she doesn't have a  life outside of it and she's talking to  her younger self but i don't know if you  know catherine keener did we really even  need to have the d aging effect or cgi i  don't know if that was completely  necessary just kind of let her look how  she is you know and i thought that maybe  her character could have used a little  more screen time too even just to get a  little more about her motivation of what  she does so she's not too  one-dimensional as a villain now i love  in this final battle scene we get  the tease about the lightsaber he has  adam and then the younger adam finally  gets to play with it and i love that  they do the superhero landing line a  shout out to deadpool obviously with  ryan reynolds that was cool i love kind  of anything ryan reynolds has that right  to break that fourth wall and kind of  step outside of the movie in our heads  and you can't go wrong with having  boston foreplay a long time playing  during that scene so good music choice  so overall i'm giving this film an 